# Lovable Master Prompt — Zoryn v1.1

Continue building this repository as a premium, customer-ready European fintech website and interactive application suite.

## Preserve the new information architecture

1. The default homepage is a public customer/corporate website, not a provider pitch.
2. Keep clear product sections for Zoryn Personal, Zoryn Business, ZorynPay, Zoryn Rewards and Security.
3. Keep the technical and provider-facing material inside the Interactive Product Centre and Platform & Operations workspace.
4. Every public call-to-action should open a useful product experience rather than a dead page.

## UI/UX standard

- Premium, calm and trustworthy fintech presentation
- Strong typography, generous spacing and accessible contrast
- Fully responsive mobile, tablet and desktop layouts
- Clear interactive states, validation, loading feedback and empty states
- Consistent Zoryn dark teal, mint and soft neutral design system
- Avoid generic template sections and unnecessary visual clutter

## Functional demo requirements

Preserve and improve all working mock flows:

- Move a user-selected amount between main balance and pots
- Move money between pots
- Validate insufficient balances
- Send mock SEPA transfers
- Issue, freeze and unfreeze cards
- Create business payment links and staff cards
- Simulate ZorynPay Tap to Pay payments
- Update settlement and transaction records
- Redeem loyalty points
- Create support cases
- Explore customer, compliance, payments and provider operations

All mock actions must continue to persist locally until Supabase is connected.

## Data layer

Use the included Supabase schema and seed files. When connecting Supabase, preserve Row Level Security and organisation-role separation. Keep regulated provider secrets server-side only.

## Provider adapters

Treat Swan and Adyen as replaceable backend adapters:

- Swan: customer/business onboarding, IBANs, accounts, balances, cards and SEPA
- Adyen: merchant onboarding, acquiring, Tap to Pay, terminals, refunds and settlements

Do not call provider secrets directly from React. Use Edge Functions or a secure backend.
